node_modules/
dist/
*.log
.DS_Store
# A skill that ships Python ships bytecode too unless this is here. Five .pyc files
# reached the index before anyone noticed, and every install would have carried them.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Run directories the Mention Network skills write into the cwd (run-dir.mjs).
# They hold a store's collected answers and meta — working artifacts, never source.
.mn-runs/
.mn-audits/

# Local state written by the why.sh hook chain, not project content: `.why-guard` and
# `.why-nudge` are per-session tokens, and `claude-activity.md` is a running log kept in the
# author's own language — one commit of it would turn the English gate red for a file nobody
# meant to publish. Scoped to those artefacts rather than to `.claude/` as a whole, so a
# project-scope `.claude/settings.json` stays checkable-in if the team ever wants one.
.claude/.why-*
.claude/claude-activity.md
